%% Mounting a Contoso share over SMB - every check the hardened account makes, in order, and where it returns STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED
%% Source: codex/playbook-enable-identity-based-auth-ad-ds.md and codex/blueprint-azure-files-secure-storage-account.md, verified on Microsoft Learn (SMB file shares in Azure Files - SMB security settings, encryption in transit, Windows client support table)
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant WS as Contoso workstation joined to contoso.local
  participant IB as Infoblox grid
  participant RES as DNS Private Resolver inbound endpoint
  participant DC as contoso.local domain controller
  participant PE as Private endpoint for the file sub-resource
  participant SA as stmryfiles01 file service
  WS->>IB: stmryfiles01.file.core.windows.net ?
  IB->>RES: privatelink.file.core.windows.net conditional forwarder
  RES-->>IB: A 10.x.x.x
  IB-->>WS: A 10.x.x.x
  WS->>PE: TCP 445 over ExpressRoute private peering
  PE->>SA: SMB negotiate, client offers its highest dialect and cipher list
  Note over SA: versions is SMB3.0 and SMB3.1.1 - SMB 2.1 was dropped, and it is refused anyway whenever Require Encryption in Transit for SMB is enabled
  SA-->>WS: dialect SMB 3.1.1 accepted
  WS->>DC: TGS request for the cifs SPN of stmryfiles01.file.core.windows.net
  DC-->>WS: Kerberos service ticket, AES-256
  WS->>SA: session setup with the Kerberos ticket
  Note over SA: authenticationMethods is Kerberos only - removing NTLMv2 is what stops account-key mounts, and kerberosTicketEncryption is AES-256 with RC4-HMAC removed
  SA->>SA: channel cipher negotiated against AES-128-GCM and AES-256-GCM
  alt client dialect, auth method and cipher are all permitted
    SA-->>WS: session established, encryption in transit satisfied
    WS->>SA: tree connect to dept-shares
    SA->>SA: share-level RBAC - Storage File Data SMB Share Contributor held by the AD-synced group
    SA->>SA: NTFS ACL evaluated on the path, as on any Contoso file server
    SA-->>WS: share mounted, all IO stays on the private endpoint
  else legacy client - Windows Server 2019 capped at AES-128-GCM, or an SMB 2.1 client, or a script still mounting with the account key
    SA-->>WS: STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED at session setup
    Note over WS,SA: the SMB security settings are checked when the session is established, not at first read - AES-256-GCM needs Windows Server 2022 or Windows 11, and a key-based mount needs NTLMv2 which is gone
    WS->>SA: retry after the fallback - restore NTLMv2 and Kerberos, move the client to an AD identity, then re-harden
  end
